WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.449 --> 00:00:10.316
The platform area is for the people who run Guildwise HQ itself. A platform administrator signs in with two-factor login and sees this separate menu.

2
00:00:11.021 --> 00:00:18.043
Organizations lists every customer, with its plan and status. You see metadata, never their work.

3
00:00:18.748 --> 00:00:25.087
Open one for its overview, its plan, limits and features, and its recent activity.

4
00:00:25.797 --> 00:00:34.052
Invitations starts a new organization: enter the owner’s email and the organization name, and they become its Owner when they accept.

5
00:00:34.756 --> 00:00:39.365
Accounts lists everyone with an account, in every organization.

6
00:00:40.074 --> 00:00:48.166
Billing holds the payment provider, the plans and their prices, the add-ons, VAT and the invoice details.

7
00:00:48.876 --> 00:00:56.688
Support is the inbox of every Contact us request. Your reply is emailed, and shows under the person’s My requests.

8
00:00:57.388 --> 00:01:00.743
Blog is where new posts wait for your review before they are published.

9
00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:08.117
API keys are for the agent API. A key is stored hashed, and shown only once.

10
00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:15.111
Runners shows the runner version this server offers. Workstations check once a day and update themselves.

11
00:01:15.811 --> 00:01:25.004
Platform team names the organization that fixes Guildwise itself. And Inbound mail sets up the provider for the mail that organizations receive.

12
00:01:25.707 --> 00:01:31.663
Finally, the Audit log records every platform administrator action, and is kept forever.

13
00:01:32.364 --> 00:01:39.829
That is the platform area: customers, money, support and the running system, kept apart from the work of each organization.
